 ability to complex natural fault zones remains uncertain. The 2018 collaps
 e of Kīlauea caldera provides a unique opportunity to test fault constitu
 tive behavior at kilometer scale\, across successive deformation cycles an
 d under highly repeatable loading. Exploring the admissible RSF parameter 
 space with a three-dimensional slider-block model\, we show that RSF fai\n
 \nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-08-08 06:45 PDT
LOCATION:Mitchell Earth Sciences
