SUMMARY:[Bioengineering] PhD Dissertation Defense: George Crowley
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260811T100000
DTSTAMP:20260808T134537Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-53613669269540-53613669269541@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Title: Simplicial Biology\n\nAbstract: In my thesis\, I used p
 hysical principles to study conserved biology across scales\, from gene ex
 pression within a single cell type up to the emergent behavior of networks
  of hundreds of millions of cells. I first showed that phenotypic variatio
 n within most human cell types is consistent with the bounds predicted by 
 Pareto optimality\, which enabled principled identification of cell functi
 on from transcriptomic data. Doing so required new software infrastructur\
 n\nAges: All ages\nSource: https://bioengineering.stanford.edu/\nLast sync
 ed: 2026-08-08 06:45 PDT
LOCATION:Clark Center
URL:https://bioengineering.stanford.edu/
END:VEVENT
